  "$comment": "PLACEHOLDER RECORDS — the work clock. Stands in for GET /api/v1/admin/team/attendance?date= (one business day, every member in scope) and GET /api/v1/admin/team/attendance/{memberId}?from&to (one member, a range). One row per member per business day, unique on (memberId, businessDate). THIS IS NOT THE AUTH SESSION: UserSession already records every login with device, UA and IP, and it is the wrong record — a person checking one number at 23:40 has logged in but has not started a shift, and a token refresh advances 'last active' whether or not anybody is at the keyboard. `businessDate` is the IST calendar date, stored beside the UTC instants and never derived from them on the client. `isLate` is COMPUTED AT OPEN against that member's own dayStartsAt + graceMinutes and stored, so changing the policy later cannot retroactively make last month late. `absent` and `unclosed` are NOT here and never will be — both are derived at read against asOf. Nothing auto-closes a forgotten day.",
